        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Annette Crosbie, David Rintoul, Ian Bannen\n- Awards: BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress, BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role\n- TV Series: The Six Wives of Henry VIII, Edward the Seventh, Doctor Finlay\n- Films: The Slipper and the Rose\n\nFacts:\n- Annette Crosbie won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for The Six Wives of Henry VIII in 1971.\n- The Slipper and the Rose is a 1976 British musical film that retells the fairy tale Cinderella.\n- Annette Crosbie won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for Edward the Seventh in 1976.\n- Annette Crosbie was nominated for the BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Supporting Role for the 1976 film The Slipper and the Rose.\n- Doctor Finlay was an ITV television series that continued the stories into the late 1940s.\n- Doctor Finlay featured David Rintoul as Dr. Finlay, Ian Bannen as Dr. Cameron, and Annette Crosbie as Janet.",
